  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Critical Relief for Independent Media in Moldova (CRIMM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the CRIMM project, Internews aims to strengthen independent media in Moldova and foster civic engagement. Seven media outlets will receive tailored support based on 2024 Media-Specific Organisational Capacity Assessments (M-OCAs), including grants and mentoring from media experts in areas like ethical reporting, AI, and revenue strategies. Endline M-OCAs in early 2026 will assess the project&apos;s progress and guide future development. In parallel, CRIMM will partner with the Independent Journalism Centre (IJC) to launch a creative content engagement fund, which will support local individuals or teams using creative storytelling and multimedia to promote civic participation, media literacy, and public discourse.</narrative>
  </description>
